00:08:43.769 --> 00:08:46.940
And open up this user data and track hubs
widget.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:50.940
I have no track hubs or other tracks right
now.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:58.610
If I want to go to that configuration menu
I go to options, and click on track hubs.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.880
Now I can search for any number of things.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:05.700
This is a very versatile search interface.

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:13.640
Let's say I want to pull up that PhyloCSF
project and I don't remember the whole name.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.840
I can use wildcards.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:22.060
So phylo asterisk and hit Go, and it finds
that project for me.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:24.220
That's a nice feature.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:31.430
Now, I check that box and again you are going
to see the list of tracks that are available

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:33.170
