00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:39.450
We have bigBed, and bigWig in this set.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:42.950
Some of these tracks are in red.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:49.360
When a provider puts together his track hub
and submits it to the registry, you can mark

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.860
a certain set of tracks as the default set.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.330
All of these in black are the defaults set.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:10:02.320
These others are not marked as default but
you can indeed load them up if you want.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:10.240
Maybe these are some type of supporting data,
for example this phylo CSF power is a measure

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:12.970
of that metric's, statistical power.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.610
That is what the red color is about.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:20.830
Here are the other assemblies I mentioned.

00:10:20.830 --> 00:10:25.430
Let's pick the phylo CSF novel set.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:28.310
So I'll check that box.

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:30.940
You get some configuration options.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:37.070
You do notice that you get this green dot,
those of you paying attention will see the

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.160
